WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.830
1966.

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.640
Two scientists take thylakoids
from spinach chloroplasts,

3
00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.310
and soak them in acid, in the dark.

4
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.490
Then, still in the dark, they
move them into an alkaline bath.

5
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.040
No light at all.

6
00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.650
Yet the thylakoids make ATP.

7
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:22.740
Mitochondria, chloroplasts and many
bacteria all make ATP with the same machine.

8
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.540
So what does that tell us?

9
00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:28.160
In this mission, you'll line up a
mitochondrion and a chloroplast,

10
00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.040
part by part, and see what matches.

11
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:35.040
Then you'll read data built
on that 1966 experiment,

12
00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.770
and decide which conclusion it supports.

13
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.800
Your mission: work out what
one shared machine tells us.
